    "['trust upstream [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet trust-zone trust', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper configuration command for `trust upstream default`:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet trust-zone trust\\n##\\n\\nNote: Juniper\\'s concept of \"trust upstream\" is typically implemented through security zones (like `trust-zone`). The exact implementation might vary depending on your security policies and device model. This translation assumes you want to mark traffic from this interface as trusted, similar to Huawei\\'s `trust upstream` functionality.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet trust-zone trust'}]]": 1,
