    "['tunnel-protocol [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls traffic-engineering tunnels', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI command `tunnel-protocol mpls te`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols mpls traffic-engineering tunnels\\n##\\n\\nThis command enables MPLS traffic engineering for tunnels on Juniper devices, which is the functional equivalent of HUAWEI's `tunnel-protocol mpls te` command that sets the tunnel protocol type to MPLS TE.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols mpls traffic-engineering tunnels'}]]": 1,
    "['destination [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path LSP-to-4.4.4.4 to 4.4.4.4', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI command `destination 4.4.4.4` for an MPLS TE tunnel:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols mpls label-switched-path LSP-to-4.4.4.4 to 4.4.4.4\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, MPLS TE tunnels are configured as Label Switched Paths (LSPs) under the `protocols mpls` hierarchy. The `to` statement specifies the destination address, similar to HUAWEI\\'s `destination` parameter. The LSP name (\"LSP-to-4.4.4.4\" in this example) would be chosen to match your naming conventions.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path LSP-to-4.4.4.4 to 4.4.4.4'}]]": 1,
