    "['mpls te service-class [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel2 class-of-service default', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper configuration command for the HUAWEI `mpls te service-class default` command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel2 class-of-service default\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, the service-class mapping is handled under the CoS (Class of Service) configuration for the LSP. The \"default\" class typically maps to best-effort forwarding (BE) in Juniper\\'s CoS system. If more precise CoS mapping is needed, additional Juniper CoS configuration would be required.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel2 class-of-service default'}]]": 1,
